@startuml leader-election
title US-07: Leader Election - One Active Evaluator Owns Rule State

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Evaluator A" as A
participant "Evaluator B" as B
database "Redis\nalert-evaluator:leader" as Redis
queue "Kafka\ndeviation.candidates +\nproximity.candidates" as Candidates

A -> Redis : SET leader instance_A NX PX TTL
B -> Redis : SET leader instance_B NX PX TTL
Redis --> A : OK
Redis --> B : nil

note over A
  Lease holder becomes active evaluator.
  It creates/joins the alert-evaluator Kafka consumer group
  and also runs the scheduled signal-loss scan.
end note

A -> Candidates : join + poll evaluator consumer group

note over B
  Follower does not join/poll the evaluator consumer group
  and does not run rule evaluation.
  It only polls/attempts lease acquisition.
end note

loop heartbeat while owner
  A -> Redis : atomic compare-and-PEXPIRE\nonly if value == instance_A
  Redis --> A : renewed or lease lost
end

note over Redis
  Exactly one lease value can exist at a time,
  but lease coordination is not exactly-once transport.
  Deterministic alert identity remains required for replay safety.
end note

@enduml
